  "partyLabels": "none-recorded",
  "note": "Triennial election of the nine Gilford Town Commissioners for 1932-35, due on 15 January 1932 (the board was told so on 14 December 1931). No nominations were lodged for the nine vacancies, so the retiring commissioners were deemed re-elected and \"the composition of the Council will remain unchanged\" (Irish News, 12 January 1932, p. 3). The paper does not name them. Five are named here: those present at the first meeting, on 23 January 1932, who signed their declarations; John Roberts was re-elected chairman there. The other four are not named in the sources found. At the same meeting David Thompson was co-opted in the room of Robert Leckey. Returned unopposed (deemed re-elected)."
